@startuml P240_oid4vci_revoke_credential

'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
' Configuration
'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
'=== Header and Footer ===
header OPEN-DID Technical Specification
footer
  	Page %page% of %lastpage% at %date("yyyy-MM-dd hh:mm:ss")
end footer

'=== Title ===
title
	<size:25>P240 : OID4VCI Credential Revocation</size>
end title

'=== Options ===
' Autonumbering: ex) "<b>000." => Display a 3-digit number with leading zeros
autonumber "<b>(#)</b>"
' Hide the participant box at the bottom of the page
'hide footbox

'=== Constants ===

!$refdoc = "Refer to separate document"
!$doc = "Refer to data specification document"

'=== Participants ===
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam BoxPadding 20
skinparam MaxMessageSize 500
skinparam MinClassWidth 80

actor "**User**" as user
box Mobile #OldLace
    participant "**Wallet**" as wal <<Wallet>>
end box

box Issuing Provider #AliceBlue
    participant "**Credential Issuer**" as ci <<Server>>
end box

participant "**Verifier**" as vf <<Server>>

box Trust Repository
    participant "**blockchain**" as BC <<Storage>> #WhiteSmoke
end box

|||
rnote over wal, ci
    This is an OpenDID OID4VCI extension API that does not use an Access Token or the TAS.
    The wallet uses the credential_revocation_endpoint and nonce_endpoint of the Issuer Metadata.
    The revocation target is identified by the Status List reference (status_list{uri, idx}) contained in the SD-JWT VC or mdoc.
end rnote

|||
== P240-1 : Request c_nonce ==

user -> wal: Request Credential revocation
activate wal
user -[#Blue]\ wal: User authentication (non-standard)
wal -> ci ++: POST {nonce_endpoint}
    ci -> ci: Generate and store c_nonce\n(valid for 10 minutes, single use)
return {c_nonce}

|||
== P240-2 : Create Revocation Token ==

wal -> wal: Extract the Status List reference of the Credential to revoke\n{status_list uri, idx}
wal -> wal: Generate Revocation Token
rnote right of wal #MintCream
    **Revocation Token (JWS)**
    header = { alg: "ES256",
               typ: "opendid-credential-revocation+jwt",
               kid: Holder DID URL }
    payload = { iss: Holder DID, iat, exp (within 5 minutes after iat),
                nonce: c_nonce,
                credential_status: { status_list: { uri, idx } } }
end note
wal -> wal: Sign with the authentication key of the Holder DID

|||
== P240-3 : Request Credential Revocation ==

wal -> ci ++: POST {credential_revocation_endpoint}
rnote right of wal #LightGray
    **[API_REQ : Credential Revocation Request]**
    revocation_token
end note
    ci -> ci: Verify token\
            \n* JWS format, header(alg, typ, kid)\
            \n* DID of kid = iss\
            \n* iat, exp (within 5 minutes, 60-second tolerance), nonce\
            \n* status_list{uri, idx} (idx >= 0)
    ci <-> BC: Retrieve / Respond Holder DID Document (iss)
        rnote right of ci #MintCream
            **DidDoc** : $doc
        end note
    ci -> ci: Verify signature\
            \n* Check that kid is a key registered in authentication\
            \n* Verify ES256 signature with the P-256 public key
    ci -> ci: Retrieve and lock issuance record\
            \n* status_list uri + idx\
            \n* Check issuance completed (ISSUED) status
    ci -> ci: Verify owner\n* subject_did of the issuance record = iss
    ci -> ci: Consume c_nonce (cannot be reused)
    alt Already INVALID
        ci -> ci: Respond with the existing change time without changing the status
    else
        ci -> ci: Change status\
                \n* VALID or SUSPENDED → INVALID\
                \n* Update Status List value and version\
                \n* Record change history (reason USER_REQUEST, changed by Holder DID)
    end
    note right of ci
        c_nonce consumption and the status change are processed in a single transaction,
        and if the status change fails, the c_nonce consumption is also rolled back.
    end note
return Credential Revocation Response
rnote right of wal #LightGray
    **[API_RES : Credential Revocation Response]**
    credential_status = { status_list: { uri, idx }, status: "INVALID" }
    revoked_at
end note
note right of wal
    **Error Responses**
    * SSRVISS00206 : Issued Credential does not exist or is not in ISSUED status
    * SSRVISS00210 : c_nonce does not exist, has expired, or has been reused
    * SSRVISS00302 : Token format / Claim / validity period error, Holder mismatch
    * SSRVISS00413 : Signature verification or public key decoding failed
end note

wal -> wal: Delete the Credential
deactivate wal

|||
== P240-4 : Check Status (Optional) ==

rnote over vf, ci
    The revocation is reflected in the Status List, and a verifier checks whether the Credential
    is revoked with the Status List reference in the Credential when the Credential is presented.
end rnote
vf -> ci ++: GET {status_list uri}
    ci -> ci: Generate and sign Status List Token
return Status List Token
rnote right of vf #MintCream
    **Status List Token** (application/statuslist+jwt)
    header = { alg: "ES256", typ: "statuslist+jwt", kid: Issuer DID URL }
    payload = { sub: status_list uri, iat, exp, ttl,
                status_list: { bits, lst } }
end note
vf -> vf: Check the status value at the idx position (INVALID = 1)

|||
@enduml
